Z||000000||ounmongk||06-10-2000||02:24 PM||||What kind of refrigerant does the Fiero use? R-12? or the new one... R34B( I think that's it). My dad has a big can of R-12 that he bought before it became banned, and he's hoping he can still use some of it. Thanks. <BR>P.S. damn, it's hot outside!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bruce||06-10-2000||02:51 PM||||The new style (R-34, or whatever) didn't become required by law until the mid-1990's. So, R-12 is the order of the day, especially if it's a hot one. Make sure you have someone qualified do the work, because it's against the law to vent the refrigerant without proper disposal equipment. Right, Ogre?||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-10-2000||02:51 PM||||stock fiero is R12 only a reworked car would have R134 in it.<P>Rigt Bruce, only licenced persons should handle the R12. There are all kinds of EPA rules for it.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 06-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||ounmongk||06-10-2000||05:12 PM||||Thanks guys, older car, that makes sense.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>My dad is EPA certified or something, got that cert. a long time ago. He'll be the one handling the charge. Thanks again, guys!  ||||reg||1
